  "title": "How Was Your Weekend?",
  "category": "social",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "level": 6,
  "order": 603,
  "theme": "friends",
  "culturalNote": "Monday morning at a Kenyan office starts with \"Wikendi ilikuwaje?\" (how was the weekend?) — and a story. Telling what happened is all past tense: -li- for what you did, -ku- for what you didn't. Object infixes let you say who it happened to without extra words: nilimwona (I saw him/her), alinipigia (she called me), tuliwaona (we saw them).",
  "startingPoint": "Monday, 9 a.m. Your colleague Wanjiku is making tea in the office kitchen.",
  "grammarFocus": [
    "past-li",
    "negative-past",
    "object-infixes"
  ],
  "grammar": [
    "past-li",
    "negative-past",
    "object-infixes",
